 "title": "Treasurer | SalineCountyMO",
 "text": "-->\nTreasurer | SalineCountyMO\ntop of page\nHOME\nElected Offices\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCircuit Clerk\nCollector\nCommission\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nProsecuting Attorney\nPublic Administrator\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nCounty Departments\nBuilding and Grounds\nEmergency Management Agency\nHuman Resources\nRoad and Bridge\nElections\nAbout Us\nMore\nCounty Links\nDirectory\nHistorical Preservation\nPrevious Office Holders\nQ & A\nVeterans Memory Walk of Honor\nMeet the Treasurer\nJared Brewer\n​\nHours:\nMonday through Friday\n8:00 am to 4:30 pm\n​\n*Office closed from 12:00 pm to 1:00 pm daily\n​\nLocation:\nSaline County Courthouse\n19 E. Arrow Street\nRoom 200\nMarshall, MO 65340\n​\nPhone:\n(660) 886-3636\n​\nFax:\n(660) 886-2644\n​\nEmail:\ntreasurer@ salinecountymo.gov\nThe County Treasurer receipts for all funds received by the county, deposits them in the bank, credits them to their proper fund within the county accounting system, then balances the account. The County Treasurer is also the Treasurer for the Schools. Jared has held this office since January 2021.\n﻿\nAll checks are signed by the County Commissioner, County Clerk, and the Country Treasurer.\n​\nThe 2024 Plat Books and the 3' x 3' County Wall Maps can be purchased from the County Treasurer's Office. The Plat Books are $35.00 each, and the Wall Maps are $50.00 each. We currently have both with and without the E911 Addresses. Items can be mailed for an additional $5.\nVeterans Memory Walk of Honor Bricks, Veteran's applications and Guardian applications can be picked up in the Treasurer's Office as well.\n﻿Mr. Brewer is assisted by Deputy Treasurer Sandy Harris.\nMonthly Sales Tax Report\nUpdated: 10/7/26\nUnclaimed Property\nThe State Treasurer is responsible for returning Missouri’s Unclaimed Property. Each year financial institutions, businesses, government agencies and other organizations turn over millions of dollars in cash and the contents of safe deposit boxes to the Treasurer’s office. The State of Missouri is approaching 1 Billion dollars in unclaimed property. One in Ten Missourians have unclaimed property.\nClick the button below to view the State of Missouri's website for unclaimed property and to file a claim\nState of Missouri Unclaimed Property\nIf you need assistance in filling out the claim forms on-line or if you want to come by the Treasurer's Office here in the Courthouse I would be glad to assist you. You might want to call prior to coming by the office to make sure I will be available to assist you. My number is 660-886-3636.\n﻿﻿© 2026 by Saline County Commission. All rights reserved.\nbottom of page",
